## Project Structure

```
agentic_mlir_qir_updated/
├── src/
│   ├── config/          # Settings and LLM configuration
│   ├── dialects/        # Extensible dialect system ✅
│   ├── parsers/         # MLIR parsing ✅
│   ├── generators/      # QIR generation ✅
│   ├── agents/          # CrewAI agents (Phase 4)
│   ├── tools/           # Agent tools (Phase 4)
│   ├── rag/             # RAG system (Phase 2)
│   ├── verification/    # Multi-backend verification (Phase 3)
│   └── ui/              # Streamlit interface (Phase 6)
├── examples/
│   ├── mlir/            # Example MLIR circuits
│   └── qir/             # Generated QIR outputs
├── knowledge_base/      # Auto-populated docs (Phase 2)
├── scripts/             # Setup and utility scripts
├── tests/               # Test suite
├── requirements.txt     # Python dependencies ✅
├── .gitignore          # Git ignore rules ✅
├── .env.example        # Environment template ✅
└── README.md           # This file
```

## Usage Example

```python
from src.parsers.mlir_parser import MLIRParser
from src.generators.qir_generator import QIRGenerator

# Parse MLIR
parser = MLIRParser()
circuit = parser.parse(mlir_code)

# Generate QIR
generator = QIRGenerator()
qir_code = generator.generate(circuit)

print(qir_code)
```

## Adding New Dialects

The extensible dialect system makes it easy to add support for new MLIR dialects:

```python
from src.dialects.base_dialect import BaseDialect

class MyDialect(BaseDialect):
    @property
    def name(self) -> str:
        return "my_dialect"

    def can_parse(self, mlir_code: str) -> bool:
        return "my_marker" in mlir_code

    # Implement abstract methods...
```

Register in [src/dialects/dialect_detector.py](src/dialects/dialect_detector.py).

## Configuration

Key settings in `.env`:

```bash
# LLM Model (choose one)
LLM_MODEL=llama3.1:8b-instruct       # Fast, 8GB VRAM
LLM_MODEL=llama3.1:70b-instruct-q4_K_M  # Best quality, 40GB VRAM

# Verification
SIMULATION_SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD=0.95
MAX_ITERATIONS=3

# IMPORTANT: Add before running!
HUGGINGFACE_TOKEN=your_token_here
```

## Testing

```bash
# Run Phase 1 test
python test_phase1.py

# Run all tests (after Phase 7)
pytest tests/
```

## Hardware Requirements

- **Minimum**: 8GB VRAM (Llama 8B), 16GB RAM
- **Recommended**: 40GB+ VRAM (Llama 70B), 32GB RAM
- **Tested on**: Intel Xeon 36 cores, 3x NVIDIA RTX 6000 (48GB each)

## Security Note

**IMPORTANT**: Before running, copy `.env.example` to `.env` and add your `HUGGINGFACE_TOKEN`. Never commit `.env` to version control!

